  "finding": "Adopted Dutch OER §§7.3–7.7 controls. Retain the first-listed Physical Chemistry route and option choices. Academic Skills first year is a zero-credit part of the 3 EC bachelor course. Formal internship preregistration is required after the first year and at least 60 EC of later study, with project approval and oral and written reports. Academic Skills exam registration is in the final year. Advanced Mechanics expects linear algebra, mechanics and waves/optics background; Electromagnetism records assumed physics and calculus background. These are distinct from formal entry restrictions. Degree-plan approval and RADAr participation do not add credits. The prospective 24/78 EC allocation is for a later year."
